ed_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"- `nvim --version`: 0.1.5 Homebrew\n- Vim (version: 7.3 Apple) behaves differently? Does not crash, but opens up the search menu by itself when iTerm loses and regains focus. Vim also rings the bell.\n- Operating system/version: OSX 10.11.6\n- Terminal name/version: iTerm2 3.0.8\n- `$TERM`: xterm-256-color\n### Actual behaviour\n\nNeovim crashes when the visible portion of a restructuredText file (439 KiB) reaches a certain point. I cannot discern the culprit exactly. The hex editor does not show any data other than plain en_US.UTF-8. The issue is there with `nvim -u NORC`.\n\nOSX mentions that Neovim crashed with a stack overflow: [nvim_2016-09-01-165612.txt](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/files/450036/nvim_2016-09-01-165612.txt)\n### Expected behaviour\n\nNeovim should not crash or behave weirdly.\n### Steps to reproduce using `nvim -u NORC`\n\nUnfortunately, due to licensing issues with the given text, I cannot really upload it for reproduction of the issue. Sorry.\n","closed_by":{"login":"justinmk","id":1359421,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTk0MjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1359421?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk","html_url":"https://github.com/justinmk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":fals